Objective

Completely redesign Seren’s menus.

The previous interface rework established a much better overall visual identity, but the menu experience itself still does not feel good enough.

The current menus feel too repetitive, too much like variations of the same panel, and not sufficiently distinctive, premium, or memorable.

I want you to rethink the complete menu experience from the ground up while preserving Seren’s current overall visual direction.

This redesign should make Seren feel like a polished standalone racing game rather than a web game displaying a succession of modal sheets.

Do not merely tweak spacing, borders, shadows, opacity, or font sizes.

Do not simply make the existing menu cards prettier.

Reconsider the compositions themselves.

Preserve the new Seren identity

