Main problem to solve

The current menu system relies heavily on one repeated structure:

* darkened backdrop
* glass container
* heading
* vertically stacked option rows
* icon on the left
* text
* chevron on the right

That pattern is useful in moderation, but it currently makes too many different decisions feel like the same screen with different text.

That needs to change.

Game mode selection, difficulty selection, player count, controller setup, race style, custom configuration, and car selection do not need to have identical visual structures merely because they are all menus.

Design each screen around the actual decision the player is making.

They should still clearly belong to the same design system, but they should not all look like clones.

Create visual rhythm across the setup flow.

Some screens can be bold and spacious.

Some can be compact and functional.

Some can emphasize visual selection.

Some can emphasize information.

Some can behave more like a dedicated game screen than a modal.

Use judgment.

